// SkyPanel7 -- the title face.
//
// Design notes, because font choice is the single biggest legibility lever at
// 64x32 and this one was iterated against the emulator's LED-dot view:
//
//  * 7px cap height. Big enough that an airline name reads at a glance from
//    across a room, small enough that three lines plus a progress bar still
//    fit in 32 rows.
//  * Single-pixel stems throughout. Two-pixel stems look bolder in a vector
//    preview and turn into mush on a P4 panel, where each LED already blooms.
//  * Uppercase only. Airline names are uppercased server-side, so lowercase
//    would be dead weight in flash; the renderer folds any that slip through.
//  * Digits are 4 wide against the letters' 5, so "24,000FT" stays compact.
//  * Contiguous 0x20-0x5A, because that is what GFXfont's first/last range
//    requires. The rarely-used symbols in the middle are cheap.
//
// Edit this file, then run `just fonts`. Never edit the generated header.

name = SkyPanel7
yAdvance = 8
baseline = 7
gap = 1

glyph 0x20 width=0 advance=2

